<title>USA: INTERVIEW - U.S. Office sees 98 sales near $5b.</title>
<headline>INTERVIEW - U.S. Office sees 98 sales near $5b.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Office Products chairman and chief executive officer said Thursday he expects the fast-growing company to have annualized sales of nearly $5 billion when fiscal 1998 ends next April.</p>
<p>Jonathan Ledecky told Reuters in an interview that he would be &quot;extremely disappointed&quot; if the company did not achieve that goal. The company's stated goal is to have $8 billion in sales annually by the end of fiscal 2000.</p>
<p>&quot;Five billion by next April is consistent with that pace,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
